164
00:09:51,860 --> 00:09:54,120
Before you design your own AI systems,

165
00:09:54,160 --> 00:09:57,580
watch out for four common mistakes that beginners often make.

166
00:09:57,620 --> 00:10:01,360
Mistake one is confusing memorization with real intelligence.

167
00:10:01,400 --> 00:10:06,220
A model that memorizes training answers may fail completely on new real world

168
00:10:06,380 --> 00:10:09,480
Mistake two is assuming sensors are always perfect.

169
00:10:09,520 --> 00:10:12,100
Real cameras get blurry in rain or glare,

170
00:10:12,140 --> 00:10:15,020
so good agents always check for uncertain readings.

171
00:10:15,060 --> 00:10:17,260
Mistake three is over engineering.

172
00:10:17,300 --> 00:10:22,460
Never use a massive neural network when five clear rules solve the problem faster

173
00:10:22,620 --> 00:10:25,420
Mistake four is ignoring physical safety limits.

174
00:10:25,460 --> 00:10:29,220
Every robot needs hard stop rules when a person comes too close.

